# build-shim.mjs's esbuild output (src/shim/node-fs.ts, pre-compiled to
# plain JS for webpack.orivon-datastore.config.cjs to alias `fs` at --
# regenerated by every `prepare.mjs --build`, never hand-edited).
#
# A NARROW re-ignore, not a reliance on the root .gitignore's own `build/`
# line: that line is immediately followed by `!build/`/`!build/icon.png`,
# negated on purpose so electron-builder's buildResources (also named
# `build/`, at the repo root) stays committed. gitignore patterns with no
# leading slash match a directory of that name at ANY depth, so that
# negation silently un-ignores this directory too -- confirmed with `git
# check-ignore` before adding this file, which is what caught it. A nested
# .gitignore is evaluated after the root one for paths under it, so `build/`
# here re-ignores THIS directory specifically without touching the root's
# own `build/icon.png`.
build/
